- F-340 **On the compiled path a folded constant at a typed place of `ZZ32`, `ZZ64`, `NN32`, `NN64`, `ZZ`, `RR64` or `RR32` is that type's constant, a float rounded once from its exact value, and a numeral as written there is its type's own coercion folded (F-347).** The coercion desugarer types a folded constant, a negative one among them, at the place's type, and leaves a numeral as written its call of the type's numeral coercion (`compiler/desugarer/CoercionDesugarer.scala`); the code generator emits the type's `make` for the first, a float from `roundToDouble` or `roundToFloat` (`compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java`, `forIntLiteralExpr`, `forFloatLiteralExpr`), and folds the coercion's body for the second, so `x: RR64 = 0.9999999999999999` is below 1.0. A place whose value is no JVM constant is a static field `numeral$coercion$N` of the component's class, filled in its static initializer, and a coercion that raises stops the program before `run()`. A place whose type names a type parameter is not hoisted (row 957). Tests: `compiler_tests/FloatNumeralOneRounding.test`, `NumeralCoercionOnceCompiled.test`, `NumeralCoercionRaisesCompiled.test`, `library_tests/NumeralFoldFloats.test`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-literal-fold/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why"; `compile-ladder/rung-static-numerals/REPORT.md`, "1. What changed and why".
- F-342 **The compiled checker converts a numeral where nothing fixes a type into its default, refuses one out of range, and refuses a numeral type written other than as a parameter's type.** Where no place's type has a coercion from the numeral's type (an untyped binding, `Any`, `Object`, `Number`, an unbounded type parameter, a receiver, a join, a result with no declared return type), a numeral becomes a `ZZ32`, or a `ZZ64` or `ZZ` by its value, or an `RR64` with a radix point. A type parameter that numerals alone fix takes the narrowest default holding them all, and the conversion into the default ranks as no coercion. A numeral outside a bounded number type's range, or rounding to an infinity, is a static error, also as a tuple's element at a tuple type and in a result position of an `if`, a `case`, a `do` block or a `try`; a program's type with no coercion from the numeral's type refuses a numeral. `NaturalNumeral` and `RadixPointNumeral` are written in a program only as a parameter's type, never as a type that an object or a trait extends. A `nat` or `int` parameter read as a value is a `ZZ32`, but a `ZZ` where it is one of a numeral coercion's four numbers (`scala_src/typechecker/staticenv/KindEnv.scala`, `getType`). It builds P-173's checker, P-174's written-only rule and four numbers, and P-40's size value; a `typecase`'s selector keeps its own numeral type (row 963). Tests: `compiler_tests/LiteralDefaultCompiled`, `LiteralDefaultResultCompiled`, `XXXLiteralTypeUnwritable.test`, `XXXNumeralBeyondZZ32Range.test`, `XXXNumeralBeyondRangeInTuple.test`, `XXXNumeralJoinBeyondRange.test`, `XXXNumeralTypeExtendedRefused.test`, `NatValueZZ32Compiled`, `NumeralStaticDesignCompiled` (a `v` beyond `ZZ64`). Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-numeral-checker/REPORT.md`, "1. What changed and why".
F-18 | start-?up|at its first us | - F-18 **On the compiled path, the class loader makes the class of a generic instantiation at its first use, by rewriting the template's bytecode with ASM, and the rewriting only renames, so it gives no instance a `double[]` field.** The class is `InstantiatingClassloader`;
F-25 | fourteen programs|atomic  | It is one of the gate's atomic runs, which run each program at four threads (`gate.md`).
F-103 | tryatomic | Detail: `explorations/compile-ladder/rung-tryatomic/REPORT.md`, "The measured defect, and its home".
F-234 | start-?up|at its first us | Removing their JVM start-up would save at most 1.8 % (P-150: no resident compiler is built).
F-259 | left of|to the left | So a tuple or `()` concatenates on the left of a string, and a function or a tuple of seven or more elements beside one raises `CastError`.
F-262 | comprises.{0,40}Numeral|e | The checker types every integer numeral by its numeral type, `NaturalNumeral[\n, r, v\]`, whose static arguments hold no sign, under the compiler's prelude and the one library alike (`scala_src/typechecker/impls/Misc.scala:469-472`), before it converts it (F-342).
F-341 | rounds? to an infinity|ou | a numeral out of the type's range, at a type with no coercion from it, or outside its coercion's `where` clause is refused there when it runs;
P-173 | rounds? to an infinity|ou | At a typed place the conversion is exact or rounds once (P-76, P-172), and a numeral outside the type's range is refused statically;
P-174 | comprises.{0,40}Numeral|e | Rows 960 and 974 hold where the tree departs: the digit count of `00.5`, and walk running a numeral type written as a static argument or as a type that an object or a trait extends.
P-175 | row (324|497|888|933|934| | the code generator evaluates a call's arguments in order (F-19, row 951), under the team's comment "Why isn't this parallel???" (`compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java:7068`), so every `SUM`, `DOT` and `BIG MAX` of microGPT would run its bodies one at a time once compiled programs run the one library.
P-175 | row (324|497|888|933|934| | It needs a group of forked arms to join every arm before it completes abruptly, which the compiled path does not do (`CodeGen.genParallelExprs` joins on the normal path only, row 947;

